&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;As the Business Affairs Associate I, you will review, negotiate, and draft business terms, and manage agreements with domestic and international licensees for our Consumer Products team, which focuses on extending the growing slate of anime brands that Crunchyroll represents into physical/digital products and experiences.&amp;nbsp;You will strategically negotiate and review agreements by balancing appropriate financial terms, legal risks, and business risks. You will work in partnership with our Consumer Products Group, as well as Legal, Finance, and other global stakeholders, to license merchandising rights for our content to domestic and international licensees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will draft and&amp;nbsp;negotiate merchandise licensing agreements with domestic/international licensees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will work closely with the Consumer Products Team and Legal Team to ensure that all negotiated terms and requirements are reflected in the agreement, and that all licensee activities and brand representation align with what has been granted and approved by the IP holders in Japan.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will escalate any unusual or high-risk provisions to internal departments, including the Consumer Products Group, the Content Team, Legal, Finance, and international affiliate companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will maintain an organized system for tracking deal terms and update negotiation statuses within our internal tracking systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will provide general business affairs support in a rapidly changing business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will document, innovate, and adapt standard operating procedures on a continual basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the role of Business Affairs Associate I, you will report to the VP, Business Affairs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are considering applicants for the location of Los Angeles, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
