&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by fans, Crunchyroll delivers the art and culture of anime to a passionate community. We super-serve over 100 million anime and manga fans across 200+ countries and territories, and help them connect with the stories and characters they crave. Whether that experience is online or in-person, streaming video, theatrical, games, merchandise, events and more, it’s powered by the anime content we all love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team, and help us shape the future of anime!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Delivery Operations Coordinator supports Crunchyroll’s global content distribution workflows, ensuring on-time, accurate delivery of video, audio, subtitles, artwork, and metadata to partners, licensors, and internal systems. This role provides cross-timezone coverage between U.S. and India, working closely with Media Operations, Production Management, and third-party vendors to monitor storefronts, validate material readiness, and coordinate outbound deliveries for both owned-and-operated (O&amp;amp;O) and partner platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and track outbound deliveries to partners such as Delta, GCD, and licensors, ensuring timely and accurate file submissions across multiple time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily delivery operations aligned to partner deadlines and content cycles (e.g., Delta Studio monthly cycles, GCD content updates, licensor drops).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate that all delivery elements meet required technical specs (e.g., video format, audio layout, subtitles, metadata, and artwork).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the liaison between Media Ops, Production Management, and external vendors (e.g., Sony Panama, Touch, IFEC providers) to troubleshoot issues and confirm delivery success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain delivery trackers and Airtable records to ensure all deliverables are logged and auditable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct daily storefront checks to confirm availability, metadata accuracy, and subtitle/audio alignment on live platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate and document storefront discrepancies such as missing assets, incorrect territories, or metadata mismatches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform material readiness checks ahead of publish or delivery deadlines to verify all required assets are approved, QC’d, and available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide overlapping coverage between U.S. and Hyderabad to ensure near-continuous delivery oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global teams to hand off ongoing tasks and ensure end-to-end visibility for each delivery window.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support EST shift coverage to align with vendor and partner business hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of experience in digital media operations, delivery coordination, or content servicing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient in asset management, storage, and systems, including familiarity with cloud-based storage solutions and file transfer protocols (e.g., AWS S3, GCP, FTP, or Aspera).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of video/audio/subtitle file types, and metadata packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have knowledge of industry-standard video editing software such as Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, or Avid Media Composer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and communication skills, with the ability to track multiple concurrent deliveries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tools like Airtable, Aspera, GCP, and content management systems preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and proactive problem solver who can work independently across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with anime, entertainment, or streaming media is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
