&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by fans, Crunchyroll delivers the art and culture of anime to a passionate community. We super-serve over 100 million anime and manga fans across 200+ countries and territories, and help them connect with the stories and characters they crave. Whether that experience is online or in-person, streaming video, theatrical, games, merchandise, events and more, it’s powered by the anime content we all love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team, and help us shape the future of anime!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Designer – Collectibles Marketing is a key creative role responsible for shaping how fans discover, engage with, and connect to Crunchyroll products across marketing, retail, and experiential touchpoints. Reporting to the Art Director, this role supports the creative execution for a wide range of fan-facing initiatives, spanning digital marketing, e-commerce, retail environments, and physical product experiences (excluding packaging).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is highly execution-focused and ideal for a designer who thrives on bringing ideas to life through compelling visuals, thoughtful design, and polished presentation materials. The Designer works across multiple mediums and projects simultaneously, creating high-quality assets that support business goals while delivering exceptional fan experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the role of Designer, you will report to the Art Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are considering applicants for the location(s) of Dallas, TX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Areas of Responsibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create custom product mockups, photorealistic product renderings, sales materials, and presentation decks that communicate product concepts and creative intent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop original visualizations and product imagery from scratch rather than relying solely on existing templates or stock mockup solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture, edit, retouch, and optimize product photography and other visual assets for use across marketing, e-commerce, sales, and retail channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute marketing and product-driven creative across digital, retail, and experiential channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design multi-channel marketing assets including email campaigns, social content, paid media, e-commerce visuals, sales presentations, and retail collateral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute creative concepts and design execution for merchandise and product development initiatives, including soft goods and hard goods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design in-store signage, displays, event graphics, and experiential assets that support product launches, brand activations, and retail storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner effectively with Product Development, Marketing, eCommerce, Sales, Operations, and external vendors through clear communication, incorporating feedback thoughtfully, and maintaining strong collaborative relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage projects end-to-end, including timelines, feedback loops, revisions, and final delivery, while working independently and maintaining a high level of accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+&amp;nbsp; years of graphic design experience, with a strong focus on marketing, product, or experiential design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3+ years of experience in layout, typography, visual storytelling, and brand consistency across both digital and physical formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience creating custom product mockups, product imagery, and presentation materials that clearly communicate ideas and elevate creative concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with product photography, photo retouching, compositing, and image manipulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience independently managing multiple projects from concept through final execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience communicating effectively with cross-functional partners and can confidently present your work and rationale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient in Adobe Creative Suite, particularly Illustrator and Photoshop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hold a Bachelor’s degree or BFA in Graphic Design or a related field, or equivalent professional experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Creative Team is a well-established group of seasoned professionals dedicated to empowering fans to own premium collectibles. We collaborate closely with Product Development, Operations, and Sales to design and market high-quality items—including home video, apparel, accessories, and home goods—on a global scale. With experts in Production, Editorial, and Design across North America, Australia/New Zealand, the UK, France, and Germany, we push creative boundaries to deliver exceptional products that fans treasure. Our goal is to continuously elevate the Global Collectibles business and set new standards in fan engagement through thoughtful, beautifully crafted design.&lt;/p&gt;
