&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by fans, Crunchyroll delivers the art and culture of anime to a passionate community. We super-serve over 100 million anime and manga fans across 200+ countries and territories, and help them connect with the stories and characters they crave. Whether that experience is online or in-person, streaming video, theatrical, games, merchandise, events and more, it’s powered by the anime content we all love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team, and help us shape the future of anime!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Frontend Engineer to help build and evolve Crunchyroll&#39;s connected-device applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will develop and maintain high-performance streaming experiences on Roku while contributing to shared client architecture, reusable application frameworks, and cross-platform capabilities used across connected devices. You will collaborate closely with product managers, designers, QA engineers, and fellow software engineers to deliver scalable, reliable, and user-focused experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong development experience with modern software engineering practices and a solid understanding of TypeScript, client-side application architecture, and maintainable frontend systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the role of Software Engineer II, Frontend, you will report to the Senior Engineering Manager, LRX Core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are considering applicants for the location(s) of San Francisco, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We get excited about candidates, like you, because you have...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional software development experience building production applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and maintaining large-scale client-side applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in TypeScript and modern JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable applications using modern frontend frameworks such as React, Vue, Angular, or similar technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of application architecture, state management, modular design, and reusable component patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and optimize Living Room applications while contributing to scalable client-side solutions that improve maintainability and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to reusable libraries, application frameworks, tooling, and architectural patterns that reduce duplication and improve consistency across applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, provide constructive feedback, and maintain high standards for code quality, testing, reliability, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, troubleshoot, and resolve complex issues across application layers, including platform-specific behavior, performance bottlenecks, and production incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize application startup time, memory usage, responsiveness, and playback experiences across connected-device environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance and mentorship to other engineers while helping improve team processes, technical standards, and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain clear technical documentation for systems, architecture decisions, development workflows, and feature implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Fan Experiences team at Crunchyroll plays a pivotal role in enhancing and expanding our users&#39; experiences. We partner with platform engineers, designers, and product teams to build immersive, performant applications that delight users across a growing range of devices. Our team thrives on action, innovation, and a shared commitment to raising the bar. We are curious, data-driven, and passionate about continuously improving the way fans experience anime.&lt;/p&gt;
