&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by fans, Crunchyroll delivers the art and culture of anime to a passionate community. We super-serve over 100 million anime and manga fans across 200+ countries and territories, and help them connect with the stories and characters they crave. Whether that experience is online or in-person, streaming video, theatrical, games, merchandise, events and more, it’s powered by the anime content we all love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team, and help us shape the future of anime!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Vice President, Content Protection &amp;amp; Anti-Piracy to define and lead our global strategy for protecting one of the world&#39;s largest anime libraries and the intellectual property that powers our business. Reporting to the General Counsel, you&#39;ll shape how Crunchyroll combats digital piracy and enables secure global distribution. You&#39;ll establish the long-term vision, operating model, technology roadmap, and strategic partnerships that help us stay ahead of evolving threats while supporting the continued growth of our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Crunchyroll&#39;s global content protection and anti-piracy strategy aligned with our long-term business and content distribution goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the vision, operating model, technology roadmap, and investment priorities for protecting Crunchyroll&#39;s intellectual property worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise executive leadership on piracy trends, enterprise risk, regulatory developments, and strategic opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new technologies, AI-enabled enforcement capabilities, and industry best practices to continuously strengthen our approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Crunchyroll&#39;s global content protection organization and day-to-day anti-piracy operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external enforcement partners responsible for notice generation, investigations, intelligence gathering, software development, and unauthorized content detection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive scalable enforcement across websites, streaming platforms, social media, search engines, cyberlockers, and other online services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Legal, Product, Engineering, Content Operations, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Security, and Sony Pictures Entertainment to improve enforcement capabilities and operational effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strategic relationships with digital platforms, hosting providers, registrars, CDN providers, payment processors, and industry organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct investigations into piracy ecosystems, monitor evolving threats, and recommend proactive strategies to reduce infringement and mitigate future risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive reporting, dashboards, KPIs, and analytics that measure enforcement effectiveness, return on investment, and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic guidance on global copyright laws, DMCA processes, platform enforcement programs, and industry best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support executive initiatives and special projects related to protecting Crunchyroll&#39;s intellectual property&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are considering applicants available to work a hybrid schedule, with three days each week onsite at our Los Angeles office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We get excited about candidates, like you, because...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience leading content protection, anti-piracy, digital rights management (DRM), trust &amp;amp; safety, intellectual property enforcement, or related programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior leadership experience within global streaming, media, or entertainment companies, building and scaling enterprise content protection programs that support worldwide content distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience developing and leading global content protection or anti-piracy strategies, including setting long-term vision, influencing executive leadership, and driving cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading global teams, managing external vendors and strategic partners, and building strong relationships across complex organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of global copyright law, DMCA processes, platform enforcement programs, digital content distribution, online piracy, and the broader internet ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading investigations into unauthorized content distribution and developing proactive strategies that improve enforcement effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with industry enforcement platforms, including YouTube Content ID, Meta Rights Manager, and Google Trusted Copyright Removal Program (TCRP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, executive communication, and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate complex legal and technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent professional experience. Degrees in Computer Science, Information Technology, Criminal Justice, Data Science, Business, or related disciplines are preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor or advanced degree in Law, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Data Science, Business Administration, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital fingerprinting technologies, content recognition systems, DRM, media asset protection, OSINT techniques, cyber investigations, domain and hosting infrastructure, CDN technologies, or online payment ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building executive dashboards and measuring program effectiveness through data and analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with major digital platforms, hosting providers, and industry organizations supporting copyright enforcement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you will love working at Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to getting to work with fun, passionate and inspired colleagues, you will also enjoy the following benefits and perks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive a great compensation package including salary plus performance bonus earning potential, paid annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible time off policies allowing you to take the time you need to be your whole self.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous medical, dental, vision, STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Saving Account HSA program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health care and dependent care FSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan, with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer paid commuter benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support program for new parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet insurance and some of our offices are pet friendly!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
